Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

## 1. Before/After Every Test in a Class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task PlaceOrder_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once Before/After All Tests in a Class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Test1() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 3. Once Per Assembly (before/after all tests in the assembly)

```csharp
public class WireMockHook
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StartAsync();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StopAsync();
    }
}
```

## 4. Once Per Entire Test Session (global start/end)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task Migrate(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrator.ApplyAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrator.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

**Key points:**

| Scope | Attribute | Method must be |
|-------|-----------|----------------|
| Per-test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | Instance |
| Per-class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | `static` |
| Per-assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | `static` |
| Per-session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | `static` |

All hooks can be `async Task` and optionally accept a context object and/or `CancellationToken`.

**Bonus:** Use `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (static, in any class) to add a cross-cutting hook that fires for *every* test in the entire run — handy for global logging or timing without touching each test class.
